The altitudes of execution: A4 swarm: agents of agents; starts and schedules other agents. A3 agent: a loop with an environment: memory across runs, its own wake, reach beyond its sandbox. A2 loop: a closed agentic loop: calls a model and uses tools until one task is done, then stops; cannot start others or schedule. A1 LLM call: one prompt in, one answer out; no tools. A0 compute: code that runs, no model.
This board item is a whole project. Cut it into 3 to 8 units of work, each at ONE altitude (the lowest that suffices), with the capability primitives it needs (verb.object.reach, e.g. read.file.project, write.repository.project, send.endpoint.allowed). Answer only JSON: {"units":[{"unit":"<what>","altitude":"A0|A1|A2|A3","grant":["..."]}],"agent_needed":true|false}
